#description: A schema in the text refers to a definition in another package of the author's module, which the text imports. A package that is not one of CUE's builtins is ref-import.
#expect: E0143
#spec: docs/invariants.md:116-120, docs/invariants.md:222
#at: lin.h
-- in.cue --
import "github.com/sdboyer/thema"

lin: h: thema.Lineage & {name: "h"}
-- text.cue --
import "example.com/m/common"

schemas: "0": "0": schema: {c?: common.#Color}
-- common/common.cue --
package common

#Color: "red" | "blue"
-- out/together/bind --
verdict: E0143
E0143 c in schema 0.0 refers to #Color, in package "example.com/m/common", which is not one of CUE's builtin packages @ /m/text.cue:4:33
